// The terminal's cursor inside `>>|` (D-16, DIS-ZYE-004 in ZyEdit/HALLAZGOS.md).
//
// `>>|` hides it. `>>~ (row, col)` with nothing to print shows it there, and
// every frame shown afterwards ends with it moved back there and shown, whatever
// the frame drew elsewhere: the second frame draws on row 2 and still leaves
// the cursor at row 1, column 6. `>>~ (0, 0)` hides it, and a frame after that
// ends with nothing about the cursor. Drawing moves the terminal's cursor, so
// the only way to see where the user sees it is the bytes, in order.
>>| {
    >>!
    >>~ (1, 1) > "hello"
    >>~ (1, 6)
    <<| k
    >>~ (2, 1) > "key " #|k|
    <<| _y
    >>~ (0, 0)
    >>~ (3, 1) > "hidden"
    <<| _q
}
